measurement_contractNote_TiiHomogeneous=CONTRACT section 7 'T_ii = g_ii (S U' - U) (isotropic)': in this field T^i_i = S U' - U holds exactly for the six transverse directions 1,2,3,5,6,7; along x0 (the direction of the plane wave) T^0_0 = S U' - U - K_0 with K_0 = i K Psibar gamma^0 Psi, so isotropy requires K = 0.
